Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Figure 3B - Revised (annotated, CSF total tau)", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"1564177f-5d6f-4cda-8119-ce174d450200"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Supersedes the original Figure 3B cell for publication. Three changes. (1) \
TAU is relabelled CSF Total Tau. (2) fluxCapMetrics used \"AC.22.6.|\" with a \
trailing pipe -- that column does not exist (0 numeric values against 156 for \
AC.22.6.), so the entry silently collapsed to Median[{}] and the panel lost \
its omega-3 DHA acylcarnitine; the published panel DOES show it at p = \
2.2e-9, matching the corrected key at 2.15e-9, so the original cell had \
drifted from the code that made the figure. (3) p-value brackets and the \
purple omega-3 sublabels are generated rather than added by hand in Keynote. \
Two cohorts (TL/BR), matching the published panel; Tom's original cell passes \
all four.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9ee7ab75-5c15-4de0-844a-7bb7c9010fd6"],

Cell["\<\
(* Figure 3B. TL versus BR for each marker, two-sided KS test (a priori \
markers, uncorrected). CD44 and CHI3L1
   are members of the astrogliosis cluster and CE.22.6 and CE.20.5 of the \
phospholipids|plasmalogens 22.6 cluster;
   the cluster PC1s identified the axes, and these tests show which \
individual members carry them.
   Exports Fig3b.png/.pdf. *)
DiceConfig[{\"Cog\" -> \"Q3\", \"Omics\" -> \"PL\"}, {\"Q3\", \"3\", \"7\"}];
labels3b = Append[brainLabelsNL, \"AC.15.0...A.\" -> \"AC.15.0\\n...A.\"];
fluxCapMetrics = Join[{\"HIP\", \"TAU\", \"CD44\", \"CH3L1\"},
  {\"GFAP\", \"GAS6\"} /. SomascanRevLookup,
  {\"AC.22.6.\", \"AC.20.5.\", \"AC.13.0.\", \"AC.15.0...A.\",
   \"CE.22.6.\", \"CE.20.5.\", \"CE.16.0.\", \"CE.17.0.\"}];
showKspQ = False; apoe4 = \"ALL\";
cc3b = Quiet[CohortComp[KeyTake[quadColorExp, {\"TL\", \"BR\"}],
   GetQuery[{\"APOE4\" -> apoe4}, coreData],
   <|\"norm\" -> \"TL\", \"ref\" -> \"TL\", \"comp\" -> \"BR\",
     \"prefix\" -> \"ADAS13 Q3 Markers:  Astrogliosis / \
Phospholipids|Plasmalogens 22.6\"|>,
   fluxCapMetrics, 1, False, labels3b, {0, 7}, True, False, {\"HIP\"}]];
cc3b = Join[cc3b, <|\"normRef\" -> \"TL\", \"showN\" -> False|>];
fig3b = UHchart[cc3b, {\"TL\", \"BR\"}, labels3b, {0, 7},
  \"ADAS13 Q3 Markers:  Astrogliosis / Phospholipids|Plasmalogens 22.6\",
  {{\"TL\", \"BR\"}}, {\"TL\", \"BR\"}, 0.375, 1/2, <||>,
  {{{\"AC.22.6.\"}, \"omega3\", \"DHA\"}, {{\"AC.20.5.\"}, \"omega3\", \
\"EPA\"},
   {{\"CE.22.6.\"}, \"omega3\", \"DHA\"}, {{\"CE.20.5.\"}, \"omega3\", \
\"EPA\"}}];
Export[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"Fig3b.png\"}], fig3b, \
ImageResolution -> 300];
Export[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"Fig3b.pdf\"}], fig3b];
fig3b\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"20a702de-63d3-4802-9c45-99ac4c763b08"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Figure 3C - Revised (annotated)", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"55aed90b-ce54-4e82-b205-ad9f40641829"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Nightingale HDL panel with generated p-value brackets and the spanning purple \
lipoprotein-class sublabels. XL.HDL spans two columns, which is why UHchart \
shifts a multi-column sublabel rather than centring it on one column. \
p-values reproduce the published panel exactly: 0.0019, 0.0044, 0.0046.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c12aff8b-7b03-4079-bd35-ea029f731197"],

Cell["\<\
DiceConfig[{\"Cog\" -> \"Q3\", \"Omics\" -> \"PL\"}, {\"Q3\", \"3\", \"7\"}];
showKspQ = False;
cc3c = CohortComp[KeyTake[quadColorExp, {\"TL\", \"BR\"}], coreData,
   <|\"norm\" -> \"TL\", \"ref\" -> \"TL\", \"comp\" -> \"BR\",
     \"prefix\" -> \"ADAS13 Q3 Markers:  Nightingale HDL\"|>,
   {\"HDL3.C\", \"XL.HDL.C\", \"XL.HDL.CE\"}, 0.005, False, brainLabels, {0, \
3}];
cc3c = Join[cc3c, <|\"normRef\" -> \"TL\", \"showN\" -> False|>];
UHchart[cc3c, {\"TL\", \"BR\"}, brainLabels, {0, 3},
  \"ADAS13 Q3 Markers:  Nightingale HDL\",
  {{\"TL\", \"BR\"}}, {\"TL\", \"BR\"}, 0.375, 1.0, <||>,
  {{{\"HDL3.C\"}, \"HDL3\",
    \"small,\\nnascent HDL;\\nhigh cholesterol efflux\\ncapacity\"},
   {{\"XL.HDL.C\", \"XL.HDL.CE\"}, \"XL.HDL\",
    \"large,\\nsaturated HDL;\\nlow cholesterol efflux\\ncapacity\"}}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8b735e51-ed38-411a-800c-4d28bed36206"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Supplementary Figure 3 - Q3 ANLS/Glycolysis, CSF Total Tau", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7eb5e016-093b-46a0-83f3-72d9db672248"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
No cell in Tom's notebook generated this panel. Four quadrants, TAU only, \
normalised to Median[BL], range 0-5. The published version carries TWO \
brackets and only one of them is a CohortComp ref/comp pair, which is why \
UHchart runs its own KS per comparison: TL vs BR = 3.5e-12 and BR vs BL = \
8.7e-14, both reproducing the published values exactly. This is the panel \
behind the Results claim of a 65% higher CSF tau in BR versus TL (computed \
+64.9%).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9c4404a8-0132-4c3d-bc64-7b34c73e0bc7"],

Cell["\<\
DiceConfig[{\"Cog\" -> \"Q3\", \"Omics\" -> \"PL\"}, {\"Q3\", \"4\", \"7\"}];
showKspQ = False;
ccS3 = Quiet[CohortComp[KeyTake[quadColorExp, {\"TL\", \"TR\", \"BR\", \
\"BL\"}],
   GetQuery[{\"Cog\" -> \"Q3\"}, coreData],
   <|\"norm\" -> \"BL\", \"ref\" -> \"TL\", \"comp\" -> \"BR\",
     \"prefix\" -> \"ADAS13 Q3 \\[Dash] ANLS|Glycolysis\"|>,
   {\"TAU\"}, 1, False, brainLabels, {0, 5}, True, False, {}]];
ccS3 = Join[ccS3, <|\"normRef\" -> \"BL\", \"showN\" -> True|>];
UHchart[ccS3, {\"TL\", \"TR\", \"BR\", \"BL\"}, brainLabels, {0, 5},
  \"ADAS13 Q3 \\[Dash] ANLS|Glycolysis\",
  {{\"TL\", \"BR\"}, {\"BR\", \"BL\"}}, {\"TL\", \"BR\"}, 0.375, 1.0]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d32f7272-dfa6-425e-93d1-ea920719a6ca"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Figure 3E - Revised (CSF total tau, single legend, trend lines)\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e85b369e-8988-4b4e-b22c-ffde37107093"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Supersedes the original Figure 3E cell. Four changes, none affecting the \
data. (1) brainLabels passed as the eighth argument so the colour legend \
reads CSF Total Tau rather than TAU. (2) One legend at the right of the row \
instead of one per panel. (3) Trend line and p-value inset restored (0.0380, \
0.00733, 0.000315). (4) Grid rather than Row, because Row wraps at page \
width, and a uniform 72pt left pad so all three frames are the same width -- \
verified at 987px each on the 300dpi export. 72pt is set by this figure's \
widest labels, the 300 000 ticks on CE.22.6.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f263ca5e-1aea-4043-80b1-be25f66734a8"],

Cell["\<\
thisData = GetQuery[{\"Cog\" -> \"Q3\", \"Omics\" -> \"PL\"}, coreData];
thesePairs = {{\"LDHB\", \"CE.22.6.\"}, {\"SMOC1\", \"AC.22.6.\"},
              {\"1433Z\", \"PE.O.16.0.22.6.\"}};
pad = {{72, 3}, {45, 10}}; imw = 312;
Legended[
 Grid[{UHpanel[#, \"TAU\", thisData, \"ADAS13 Quartile 3\", brainLabels, pad,
      imw] & /@ thesePairs}, Spacings -> {0, 0},
   Alignment -> {Center, Center}],
 UHlegOf[PubScatter[Last[thesePairs], \"TAU\", thisData, {Cyan, \
Darker[Blue]},
    <||>, Automatic, \"ADAS13 Quartile 3\", brainLabels]]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"125b5a60-8dd8-4a04-8019-112b33db0c26"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Closed]],

