Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gene Summaries", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1a24ce61-fdb8-40a6-a73f-c93c0350e8f6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["INPP5D (rs10933431)", "Subitem",ExpressionUUID->"afd1e43d-a649-40ad-bc48-56c16c5bfd0b"],

Cell["\<\
The gene INPP5D encodes the protein SHIP1 (SH2 domain-containing inositol 5\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]-phosphatase 1), which plays several roles in cellular \
signaling, particularly in immune cells. While SHIP1 is primarily known for \
its function in immune regulation, it can also influence cholesterol \
metabolism through various indirect mechanisms. Here are some ways SHIP1 \
might play roles in cholesterol metabolism:\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"8f87000e-d9c9-4c1c-877b-e493afbf1012"],

Cell["\<\
SHIP1 negatively regulates the PI3K/Akt signaling pathway by \
dephosphorylating phosphatidylinositol (3,4,5)-trisphosphate (PIP3). The \
PI3K/Akt pathway is critical for various cellular processes, including lipid \
metabolism. By modulating this pathway, SHIP1 can influence the synthesis and \
storage of lipids, including cholesterol.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"d0209fd5-9326-4d7a-9b51-5be1c10d6280"],

Cell["\<\
Hazen AL, et al. \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]SHIP is a crucial regulator of \
macrophage signaling and function.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] J Exp Med. 1999.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"3e3bfb9e-a578-4f58-8511-b79b4ccce076"],

Cell["\<\
Liu Q, et al. \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]The SH2 domain-containing inositol 5\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]-phosphatase 1 (SHIP1) regulates cell polarization and \
motility.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] J Cell Biol. 2000.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"3e216aea-9baa-40c8-afbe-a2cd2cf09cd8"],

Cell["\<\
SHIP1 is highly expressed in macrophages and plays a significant role in \
their function. Macrophages are crucial for cholesterol homeostasis as they \
can uptake, process, and export cholesterol. SHIP1 influences the signaling \
pathways that regulate the expression of ATP-binding cassette transporters \
(e.g., ABCA1 and ABCG1), which are essential for cholesterol efflux from \
macrophages to high-density lipoproteins (HDL).\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"8006dfad-f736-4244-b446-634b160f3ac9"],

Cell["\<\
Varin A, et al. \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]SHIP-1 and the negative control of \
immune responses.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Immunol Res. 2006.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"9229f6a5-4a62-41ca-92ed-a5fcc3e07300"],

Cell["\<\
Heit B, et al. \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]SHIP-1-deficient mice reveal a critical \
role for SHIP in regulating inflammatory responses.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
Biochem Biophys Res Commun. 2002.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"2ac701af-e315-46fc-a982-a1454ea2d3b6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["TNIP1 (rs871269)", "Subitem",ExpressionUUID->"1dea28ff-f252-4543-94c0-4f31549ca873"],

Cell["\<\
The gene TNIP1 (TNFAIP3 Interacting Protein 1) encodes the protein \
A20-binding inhibitor of NF-kappaB activation 1 (ABIN-1).\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"4ea0d36b-e3d1-4581-b762-f936594a9159"],

Cell["\<\
Macrophage Cholesterol Efflux: Macrophages play a critical role in \
cholesterol metabolism through the uptake and efflux of cholesterol. The \
regulation of NF-\[Kappa]B by TNIP1 in macrophages can influence the \
expression of genes involved in cholesterol efflux, such as ATP-binding \
cassette transporters (ABCA1 and ABCG1).\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"4713030a-685e-4278-b2af-6181222e5e0e"],

Cell["\<\
Verstrepen, L., Bekaert, T., & Beyaert, R. \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Inflammatory signaling and TNIP1.\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Cytokine & Growth Factor Reviews. 2008.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"5f4e5e38-1d67-454e-986d-c1eb66b45166"],

Cell["\<\
Baker, R.G., Hayden, M.S., & Ghosh, S. \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NF-\[Kappa]B, \
inflammation, and metabolic disease.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Cell Metab. 2011.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"5fef1fb6-8f19-4aed-8380-c6d4958cc4a8"],

Cell["\<\
CYP7A1 Regulation: CYP7A1 (cholesterol 7\[Alpha]-hydroxylase) is the \
rate-limiting enzyme in the classical pathway of bile acid synthesis. \
Inflammatory cytokines can downregulate CYP7A1 expression via NF-\[Kappa]B \
signaling. By inhibiting NF-\[Kappa]B, TNIP1 may help maintain CYP7A1 \
expression and proper bile acid synthesis.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"26ff4682-910d-45b7-8db0-26c32073b932"],

Cell["\<\
Chiang, J.Y.L. \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Regulation of bile acid synthesis: \
pathways, nuclear receptors, and mechanisms.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] J \
Hepatol. 2004.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"eedd8034-f9e7-4a9e-8877-2a3e11bda666"],

Cell["\<\
Li, T., & Chiang, J.Y.L. \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Regulation of bile acid and \
cholesterol metabolism by PPARs.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] PPAR Res. 2009.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"e3cc5635-da2f-4426-8609-ba071acddf65"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["PICALM (rs867611,rs561655)", "Subitem",ExpressionUUID->"4322436f-358b-4130-8b20-c544d853dc0b"],

Cell["\<\
PICALM (phosphatidylinositol-binding clathrin assembly protein) plays a role \
in cholesterol metabolism by influencing the trafficking and processing of \
cholesterol within cells. Here\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a detailed overview of its \
functions:\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"a1f455a5-d837-4ae9-8817-d3718c98c164"],

Cell["\<\
By regulating intracellular cholesterol trafficking, PICALM can impact the \
availability of cholesterol for CYP27A1. Efficient transport mechanisms \
ensure that cholesterol reaches the mitochondria, where CYP27A1 is located.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"527cefad-151e-4bd3-b4ed-e56170f6c2cb"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["TSPOAP1 (rs2632516,rs2526377)", "Subitem",ExpressionUUID->"8fa2b7ce-21db-46a7-b088-2635df8a8814"],

Cell["\<\
TSPOAP1 (Translocator Protein Associated Protein 1), also known as DBI \
(Diazepam Binding Inhibitor) or Acyl-CoA Binding Protein (ACBP), plays a \
significant role in cholesterol metabolism, particularly in the regulation of \
steroidogenesis and intracellular cholesterol transport. Here\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a detailed overview of its functions\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"6e244cc9-1de1-4d68-9c4b-d9b781dc1af3"],

Cell["\<\
TSPOAP1 interacts with the translocator protein (TSPO), a protein located in \
the outer mitochondrial membrane that is involved in the transport of \
cholesterol into mitochondria, where it is converted into pregnenolone, the \
precursor of all steroid hormones.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"5ea4d117-5df7-4b6c-aa3f-ee59333b0f52"],

Cell["\<\
TSPOAP1 is involved in the transport of cholesterol from the cytoplasm to the \
mitochondria. By binding to cholesterol, TSPOAP1 helps in its delivery to \
TSPO, which then facilitates its movement into the inner mitochondrial \
membrane.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"a002f720-d201-496c-8dd1-182451fb9605"],

Cell["\<\
As Acyl-CoA Binding Protein (ACBP), TSPOAP1 binds long-chain acyl-CoA esters \
with high affinity. This binding plays a role in intracellular lipid \
metabolism and the regulation of lipid biosynthesis.\
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"ba35331f-56eb-4b89-99c6-571f6b37088c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["SPTLC3 (rs686548)", "Subitem",ExpressionUUID->"f09ad34f-05cd-40dd-884e-aee8d4f5e324"],

Cell["\<\
The SNP rs686548 is a single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) located on the \
SPTLC3 gene, which encodes the serine palmitoyltransferase long chain base \
subunit 3, an enzyme involved in sphingolipid biosynthesis. \
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"0c1c3f42-c584-44d4-8ff1-277d9979c2d4"],

Cell["\<\
The SNP rs924135 is another single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) located in \
the SPTLC3 gene, which encodes the serine palmitoyltransferase long chain \
base subunit 3, an enzyme involved in sphingolipid biosynthesis. \
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"4e0ae40e-eb4d-4249-bb9b-ac2abb7a7099"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["NRH13 (LXRalpha) (rs3758673, rs7120118 - Q23 only)", "Subitem",ExpressionUUID->"41095a93-be6f-44d5-aa19-f2398a66f9f5"],

Cell["\<\
The SNP rs3758673 is a single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) located on the \
NR1H3 gene, which encodes the nuclear receptor liver X receptor alpha \
(LXR-alpha). \
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"1e53dcf7-e8fc-4bb7-b55d-7958fd66dba4"],

Cell["\<\
The SNP rs7120118 is a single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) located on the \
NR1H3 gene, which encodes the nuclear receptor liver X receptor alpha \
(LXR-alpha). \
\>", "Subsubitem",ExpressionUUID->"70cffeef-b50e-47f5-a8e1-58e1b332e2d6"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Closed]],

