Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Supplementary Table 7 - APOE Quadrant Breakdown (KM quadrants)\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5d8e82e8-3a20-4e3e-af55-0bcbcc12e2f9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Todd's Figure 6 ask (revision item #5): an APOE breakdown per KM quadrant. Q2 \
first to match the figure, where 6a = Q2 and 6b = Q3. Result: in Q3 epsilon-4 \
is balanced across quadrants (41-44%), so the Q3 quadrant signal is \
APOE4-independent; in Q2 epsilon-4 is enriched in BR (44.7%), so the Q2 \
quadrant effect is partly entangled with epsilon-4 and needs either a \
carrier-stratified quadrant KM, a Cox model, or a stated limitation.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2dee2567-0875-4a28-8a62-f9d2bfc5c0de"],

Cell["quadBreakdown[\"Q2\", {\"LDHB\", \"CER.D19.1.18.0.\"}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"96a96c34-48b8-4a5a-bbb6-3a19d9167a83"],

Cell["quadBreakdown[\"Q3\", {\"Q3\", \"3\", \"7\"}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ae0daa64-8aaf-415b-ba71-72b9a5dd14e5"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Supplementary Figure 6 - APOE4-Stratified KM", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"4c06b680-4f37-4382-bace-ff57cb388420"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Revision item #14. Carriers progress faster within both quartiles: Q2 \
log-rank p = 0.0012 (8 point), Q3 p = 0.0070 (6 point). Read alongside Supp \
Table 7 -- the quartile-level epsilon-4 gradient is driven by Q4 (carrier \
frequency 34.8 / 33.1 / 42.3 / 69.7% across Q1-Q4, flat across Q1-Q3, trend p \
= 0.17), so the Q3 reorganization is not an epsilon-4 dosage artefact.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c18ed222-9255-4071-b95c-f5ccdefa3c1a"],

